-- title:
--   Euler characteristic twisted by a sum of invertible ideal sheaves
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, let $\iota : Y \to X$ be a morphism of schemes and let $y : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper. Let $S$ be a finite subset of an index type $F$, let $I : F \to X.\mathrm{IdealSheafData}$ be a family of quasi-coherent ideal sheaves on $X$, and let $a, d : F \to \mathbb N$. Assume that for each $i \in S$: the ideal sheaf $I_i$ is invertible in the sense that every point of $X$ lies in some $X.\mathrm{basicOpen}\,f$, with $U$ affine open and $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$, on whose affine basic open the ideal is generated by a single non-zerodivisor; the inverse-image ideal sheaf $(I_i).\mathrm{comap}\,\iota$ on $Y$ is invertible in the same sense; the closed immersion of the subscheme cut out by $(I_i).\mathrm{comap}\,\iota$ followed by $y$ is finite; and this composite has $\mathrm{finrank}$ equal to $d_i$ at every point of $\operatorname{Spec} k$. Let $M$ be an $\mathcal O_X$-module which is invertible, i.e. each point of $X$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ with $(\,\cdot\,)|_U$ of $M$ isomorphic to the unit module of $U$, and let $\mathcal W$ be a cover of $Y$ by two affine opens $U_0, U_1$ with $U_0 \sqcup U_1 = \top$ and $U_0 \cap U_1$ affine. Write $\chi(N) := \dim_k H^0 - \dim_k H^1$ for the two-term Čech complex $\mathcal W.\mathrm{sectionsOf}\,y\,N$, whose $H^0$ is the kernel and whose $H^1$ is the cokernel of $\Gamma(N, U_0) \times \Gamma(N, U_1) \to \Gamma(N, U_0 \cap U_1)$. Put $J := \prod_{i \in S} I_i^{a_i}$. Then both $$\chi\bigl(\iota^*(J^{\vee} \otimes M)\bigr) = \chi(\iota^* M) + \sum_{i \in S} a_i d_i \quad\text{and}\quad \chi\bigl(\iota^*(J \otimes M)\bigr) = \chi(\iota^* M) - \sum_{i \in S} a_i d_i$$ hold in $\mathbb Z$, where $J$ is viewed as an $\mathcal O_X$-module via `module` (the kernel of the map from the unit module to the pushforward of the unit module along the subscheme immersion) and $J^{\vee}$ is its dual `invModule`.
--
--   This is the additivity of degree in the Riemann–Roch Euler characteristic under twisting by $\pm\sum_{i \in S} a_i D_i$, for a finite family of effective Cartier divisors $D_i = V(I_i)$ on $X$ restricted to a proper $k$-scheme $Y$, the relevant $d_i$ being the degrees over $k$ of the restricted divisors (intersection numbers when $Y$ is a component of a fibre of a regular model). Since the hypotheses are imposed only for indices in $S$, the family may be indexed by all components of a fibre while $S$ omits the one carrying $Y$; it is used in the Euler-characteristic computations on glued curves and on resolved models of modular curves.
